#### PID with TOF

The expected value of the particle velocity is calculated with a given momentum and mass assumption as

\[\beta^{part}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{1+m_{part}^{2}/p^{2}}}. \tag{3.7}\]

The velocity measurement is done from TOF and track length,

\[\beta=\frac{v}{c}=\frac{L}{ct} \tag{3.8}\]

where \(t\) is from the TOF system, _i.e._, \(t\equiv t_{stop}-t_{start}\) and \(L\) is from tracking in the TPC.

