* Obtain parameters of the electron distribution in \(n\sigma^{e}_{dE/dx}\) vs \(\Delta\beta^{-1}/\beta^{-1}\).
* Calculate the TOF matching efficiency for electrons.

##### Selection Procedure

The same event cuts are used as in the main analysis except the \(|V_{Z}(TPC)-V_{Z}(VPD)|<6\) cm cut. The \(e^{-}e^{+}\) pairs from gamma conversions are selected by applying geometric cuts.

1. Identify all possible global tracks with \(|n\sigma_{electron}|<2\) cut as well as minimum track quality cuts, nHitsFit \(>15\) points and the ratio of nHitsFit to nHitsPoss to be bigger than 0.52.
2. Select tracks among those global tracks by requiring global DCA less than 2 cm and \(0.2<p_{T}\leq 2\) GeV/\(c\) as primary track candidates, since we want the primary track electron distribution.
3. For selecting \(e^{-}e^{+}\) pairs from gamma conversions (unlike-sign pairs), calculate the pair values from all possible pairs of a primary candidate (electron or positron) and an opposite charged global track candidate.
