The Students' T distribution is defined without a normalization factor as follow

\[\left(1+\frac{\lambda(x-\mu)^{2}}{\nu}\right)^{-\frac{\nu+1}{2}}.\] (A.3)Let us define \(y\equiv\sqrt{\lambda}(x-\mu)\), \(\mathrm{d}y=\sqrt{\lambda}\mathrm{d}x\). Then the integral is

