Let us calculate \(\delta\left(\frac{\Delta\mathbf{\beta}^{-1}}{\mathbf{\beta}^{-1}}\right)\). The "\(\delta\)" symbol indicates the standard deviation of a distribution of a variable considered. So \(\delta\left(\frac{\Delta\mathbf{\beta}^{-1}}{\mathbf{\beta}^{-1}}\right)\) is standard deviation of the random variable \(\frac{\Delta\mathbf{\beta}^{-1}}{\mathbf{\beta}^{-1}}\).

Recalling

\[\frac{\Delta\mathbf{\beta}^{-1}}{\mathbf{\beta}^{-1}}\equiv\frac{\mathbf{ \beta}_{TOF}^{-1}-\mathbf{\beta}_{TPC}^{-1}}{\mathbf{\beta}_{TOF}^{-1}}=1- \frac{L}{ct}\left(1+\frac{m^{2}}{p^{2}}\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}\equiv X,\] (B.9)

