**Vita**

Masayuki Wada was born in Neyagawashi, Osaka, Japan on 24 June 1982, the son of Osamu Yamaguchi and Michiko Yamaguchi. He began to take an interest in science when he was in an elementary school because a girl he liked at the time liked stars and the universe. He received the Bachelor of Science degree in Physics from the Tokyo University of Science in 2005. In September 2006, he entered the Graduate School at The University of Texas at Austin. From 2007-2013 he worked as a graduate research assistant in high-energy nuclear experimental physics. He was a member of the STAR collaboration from 2007-2013. He mainly contributed to the maintenance and operation of the TOF detector subsystem and the development of particle identification methods using the TOF detector.

